From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:36:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: log guest device-memory allocations of 64 MiB and more
 (diagnostic)

On the RPi4 AAOS guest with HWUI on Venus, a single render-server context was
seen to hold ~600 MiB of v3d GEM the second it appeared (host memory attribution
at 1 Hz), and that burst is what pushes DomD into its reclaim livelock. This
names the request: context id and debug name, size, memoryTypeIndex and the
first pNext sType (import/export/AHB), for any vkAllocateMemory of 64 MiB or
more. Diagnostic; drop once the allocator is known.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic]
---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -234,6 +234,17 @@
    TRACE_FUNC();
    struct vkr_context *ctx = dispatch->data;
    struct vkr_device *dev = vkr_device_from_handle(args->device);
+   /* diagnostic (0019): name the big ones. On the RPi4 AAOS guest a single context
+    * was seen to take ~600 MiB of v3d GEM the moment it appeared; this says which
+    * context asked for how much, and from which memory type. */
+   if (args->pAllocateInfo && args->pAllocateInfo->allocationSize >= (64ull << 20)) {
+      const VkBaseInStructure *pnext = args->pAllocateInfo->pNext;
+      VkStructureType first = pnext ? pnext->sType : 0;
+      vkr_log("large vkAllocateMemory: ctx %u (%s) size %llu MiB memoryTypeIndex %u pNext sType %u",
+              ctx->ctx_id, ctx->debug_name ? ctx->debug_name : "?",
+              (unsigned long long)(args->pAllocateInfo->allocationSize >> 20),
+              args->pAllocateInfo->memoryTypeIndex, (unsigned)first);
+   }
    struct vkr_physical_device *physical_dev = dev->physical_device;
 
    VkMemoryAllocateInfo *alloc_info = (VkMemoryAllocateInfo *)args->pAllocateInfo;
